{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/820735-stats-for-humanesque-monsters","id":820735,"title":"stats for humanesque monsters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-31T21:50:14-08:00","id":820735,"title":"stats for humanesque monsters?","content":"watching films like the descent got me thinking. What if a good church loving dog finds, deep in a cavern, the last remaining vestiges of mankind. Devolved into cavern dwelling blind monsters. What manner of stats would creatures like that have? Not only that, but the cultural ramifications on races of intellectuals that idolize the &quot;what came before.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T01:47:35-08:00","id":822198,"title":"","content":"Well, since Pugmire is based off D20, you could always pillage stats from D&amp;D degenerate humanoids. Tweak their stats and abilities to whatever purpose you needed.<br /> <br /> If any Dogs did discover humans, devolved to primal beasts, they'd probably try to keep a lid on that. They'd also attempt to rationalize them as being what happens to those Men who fell from divinity. Fallen angels, essentially. Anything that dismisses their existence as fringe cases, not indicative of Man as a whole. Perhaps even as an object lesson, that such is the same that could happen to Bad Dogs who follow in the footsteps of Bag Men.<br /> <br /> On the whole, though, I'm wary of introducing actual humans into the game. Man is meant to be this distant progenitor, a figure of myth and legend. Larger than life beings who bent the world to their Will. Beings who are to Dog what God is to Man. Any number of rumors could be spread of Man still being around, but the instant you have one show up, the mystique is lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T17:55:08-08:00","id":822922,"title":"","content":"Yeah that whole idea goes hand in hand with a corrupt church of man that actually knows the truth and is keeping said lid on it. Including inquisition hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T02:47:17-08:00","id":823187,"title":"","content":"What if they were actually mutated chimpanzees?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T19:03:46-08:00","id":835504,"title":"","content":"that might be fun. I hadn't thought of that. I don't have stats for chimps but I can make that work. I'd imagine them to be amongst the uplifted races though. Maybe something more like Micheal Criton's Congo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T23:47:06-07:00","id":1255189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/820735-stats-for-humanesque-monsters?p=822198#post822198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Any number of rumors could be spread of Man still being around, but the instant you have one show up, the mystique is lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay! That is precisely my view. Not even chimps.<br /> <br /> No orcs, though badgers seem to be an analog, no elves, though I'd like to see some ancient sylvan race... <br /> Kolbolds you could use, particularly the dog-faced kobolds of old; the reptilian ones of today could be added to the desert wastes that the nomadic lizards inhabit.<br /> But what about the creatures of Nature that typically took humanoid form? I'm talking dryads, sylphs, and such. (some could even throw true elves in there). I'm thinking that they emulate whatever is the predominant &quot;people&quot; of the world, so because dogs and cats now are in abundance, that's what they look like.<br /> And I also like the little folk like fairies and pixies. I think it would be cool to have a little 6&quot; canine or feline-like fairy flitting about!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24594-lightjammer","name":"lightjammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}